  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Teena Thacker\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Teena Thacker</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675387/ET-Bureau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ET Bureau</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Sep 7, 2026 at 07:19 AM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                            <li>\n                                                        \n                                                            \n                                                                Read by \n                                                            \n                                                            100 Professionals\n                                                        \n                                                    </li>\n                                                                                    </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: A petition has been filed before the <a href=\"/tag/supreme+court\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Supreme Court</a> challenging the manner in which the government-backed human papillomavirus (HPV) vaccination programme is being implemented.Alleging that it violates constitutional guarantees of <a href=\"/tag/informed+consent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">informed consent</a>, bodily autonomy, transparency, and accountability, the <a href=\"/tag/public+interest+litigation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">public interest litigation</a> (PIL) has sought suspension of the school-based component of the <a href=\"/tag/hpv+vaccination\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">HPV vaccination</a> programme until a legally compliant informed consent protocol is established.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The PIL, filed by the <a href=\"/tag/universal+health+organisation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Universal Health Organisation</a>, is likely to be heard this week. \"Constitutional rights and public health objectives are complementary rather than conflicting,\" the petition said, arguing that India's vaccination programmes should be implemented in a manner that preserves both individual rights and public trust.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>The HPV vaccine is a critical tool in preventing cervical cancer, one of the leading causes of cancer deaths among women in India. India officially launched a free nationwide human papillomavirus (HPV) vaccination programme in February this year to combat cervical cancer, targeting 15-year-old girls.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The petition alleges that the programme violates the constitutional rights of parents and minor children under Articles 14 and 21 of the Constitution as it has been introduced without a lawful informed-consent framework, without adequate disclosure of risks and available alternatives, without a transparent adverse-event reporting mechanism and without any <a href=\"/tag/vaccine+injury+compensation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">vaccine injury compensation</a> scheme.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The petition also refers to the Parliamentary Standing Committee's 72nd Report of 2013, which examined alleged irregularities in an earlier HPV demonstration project conducted by PATH, arguing that similar concerns regarding informed consent must not arise in the current nationwide vaccination drive against HPV.It has also sought the constitution of an independent expert committee to examine epidemiological data, <a href=\"/tag/vaccine+safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">vaccine safety</a>, consent practices and available alternatives; the establishment of a real-time public AEFI (<a href=\"/tag/adverse+events+following+immunisation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">adverse events following immunisation</a>) surveillance dashboard, the notification of a national vaccine injury compensation scheme; and the formulation of a comprehensive vaccine consent framework governing vaccination of minors in India.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>Representatives of Universal Health Organisation said public trust in immunisation programmes is enhanced-rather than dsiminished-when transparency, informed choice and accountability are prioritised in public health policy.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Teena Thacker</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Teena Thacker</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675387/ET-Bureau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ET Bureau</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Sep 7, 2026 at 07:19 AM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Sep 7, 2026 at 07:19 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">2 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                                            <!-- <div class=\"app-store-container desktop-view\">\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"\" aria-label=\"Play Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-g-play.png\" alt=\"\" />\n                            </a>\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"App Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-app-store.png\" alt=\"\" />\n                            </a>\n                        </div>    -->\n                         \n                \n                                    <figure>\n                        <!-- <i></i>\n                        <span class=\"scan-text\">Scan to download App</span> -->\n                        <img src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/bar-codes/health_barcode.png?mod=3454\" alt=\"\">                        \n                        <!-- <span class=\"border-bottom\"></span> -->\n                    </figure>\n                            \n       \n\n\n                    \n                \n            "
